[98.653706, "o", "Jim faces potential abduction charges under Virginia Code § 18.2-47(A) in connection with his actions toward bank customer Bobby and bank tellers during the May 23, 2025 Wells Fargo Bank robbery. Based on Virginia case law, particularly the \"incidental restraint\" doctrine established in Brown v. Commonwealth and Hoyt v. Commonwealth, Jim's likelihood of conviction on separate abduction charges is LOW to MODERATE. The restraints imposed appear largely incidental to the robbery, though Bobby's situation presents the strongest case for the Commonwealth.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
